id #uuid "b63812c2-8cab-5357-92df-d66c9747bebb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299252}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cecd5cf6-ba72-50d3-91d2-17f1da2ed445" :question/math-academy-id "q-317026" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2x-3y \\\\ -4x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot x+(-3)\\cdot y \\\\ (-4)\\cdot x+0\\cdot y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2x-3y \\\\ -4x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}]}
